In his key note address during the congress, Stresemann has not only reaffirmed his allegiance to the symbols and traditions of the old imperial order but emphatically ruled out the DVP's participation in a <span style="color: var(--i-colour);">monarchist</span> countermovement on the grounds that this could only lead to civil war and make union with Austria impossible. It seems the DVP will be trying to sway our disillutioned middle class voters to defect as he is actively trying to search for a compromise between the <span style="color: var(--z-colour);">rep</span><span style="color: var(--spd-colour);">ubli</span><span style="color: var(--ddp-colour);">can</span> and <span style="color: var(--i-colour);">monarchist</span> causes.

We must toe the line between coalition unity and addressing the interests of our middle class voters, since at least for now, they are still our most numerous supporters and the SPD's agenda isn't appealing to them at all. We must find a way out of this situation, or else we will be facing massive electoral loss after the passing of the constitution.

